config FREETZ_LIB_libjemalloc
	bool "libjemalloc (libjemalloc.so)"
	default n
	help
		jemalloc is a general purpose malloc(3) implementation that emphasises
		fragmentation avoidance and scalable concurrency support.

		It is used as the allocator in Firefox, FreeBSD, and many other
		high-performance applications. Compared to the default uClibc allocator
		it provides better heap metadata management and avoids SIGFPE crashes
		caused by corrupted heap state on MIPS targets.

		https://jemalloc.net/

